            <div xml:id="d1517">

                <pb facs="1201" n="1191" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.8576/6–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-29T13:00:00+08:00">June 29, 1949—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 29—9:02 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2547. Re mytel 2539, June 29, 1 p. m. Another telephone conversation with police
                    station indicates that, as result of Foreign Affairs Bureau intercession, matter
                    has been dropped.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2547, repeated Nanking 1395.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
